      "reactions": null,
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{65389b06923e8df5f840b20c|full_name} VRChat already have something in the works that would inherently deal with Public NSFW avatars, targeting the root cause of why it is harmful. (Exposure to minors)\n\nA) Users really need to start uploading avatars that are correctly tagged, or fully expect to be banned/suspended for uploading incorrectly tagged content.\n\nB) Tagged content must be restricted from being accessed or viewed by people who are not age-verified. \n\nThe above has already been earmarked in Dev blogs, and I look forward to the full implementation of it.\n\nAs an added bonus, I feel that only Trusted Users and above should be able to upload Public Avatars to increase the cost of uploading untagged content, prevent people from doing uploads on alternate accounts etc, or just making a new account when banned and immediately going back to uploading untagged NSFW material.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
