      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{648f8f50783a43691c19c812|full_name} What would you say to someone who is sceptical that avatar creators, especially those that do 1:1 commission work such as retextures, won't:\n\nA) Start charging extra for unity files or outright just not supplying them following the implementation of this feature.\n\nB) Start using avatar permissions as a poor-man's form of DRM, revoking paid content from users who have aggrieved them in some way. (There could be valid use cases for this, granted, but saying there are valid use cases only adds to the reason that artists will start charging an arm and a leg for unity files if this is ever implemented - Payment for the reduced control over the content.)\n\nC) Start using this as a way to lock people in to paying the creator for every single edit they want, effectively turning VRChat users into cash cows in a way where VRChat's platform is directly involved, but doesn't get a cut of the transaction. (Presumably because the financial part of the transaction will occur outside VRChat)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
