      "created": "2025-03-27T12:24:03.577Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "deletedAt": null,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5ac80568eae97a2368735228",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 2
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "People concerned about creator files not being shared or prices increasing are being quite silly and in my opinion, selfish.\n\nAvatar creators can't just say \"oh well we don't have to share the files anymore, so I'm going to charge extra for that\", as people will still tend to want those files. The logical outcome will be a DISCOUNT if you don't want the source files included.\n\nThe system as it exists now is currently a HUGE BARRIER to the average user getting avatar commissions. Because it either requires them to trust you by giving you access to their account, or for them to be technical enough to upload it themselves (and then the burden of maintaining/updating that avatar if needed also becomes a bigger back-and-forth).\n\nIf all a commission required was to make the model and send them an invite to clone the avatar privately, it would make a lot more people be willing to get into it. Most people don't want their personally commissioned avatar to be public, but it has to be set public for them to clone it currently.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
