      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{627289d1f270d413d04be59f|full_name} That's already how avatars exist once exported/uploaded, so it would make more sense to just have a whitelist entry on avatar web-data that allows it to be cloned by people in that whitelist, or an option to replace the ownership values on it. As these would require just a few hours of back-end work to implement and some interface code to facilitate it.\n\nThey could even utilize the in-game notification/invite system, so a creator could, on their own time, just send a \"Invite to Take Ownership of Avatar\", and whenever that user logs in, they will see that and could choose to accept it, and now the avatar is in their account account instead.\n\nI would actually expand on this idea a bit though and have the web data contain a \"maintainer\" entry. The user defined in this entry would still have the power to upload changes to the avatar, but they would not have deletion permissions, and the \"owner\" can remove or change who the maintainer is.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
